.TH RGBEASTD 8 "September 2026" "rgbeastd 1.0.1" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
rgbeastd \- RGBeast RGB lighting daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rgbeastd
.RI [ \-\-session ]
.RI [ \-\-simulate ]
.RI [ \-\-scan ]
.RI [ \-\-state\-dir " DIR" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rgbeastd
is the only process that opens the USB HID and I2C device nodes of the
lighting controllers. It runs as the unprivileged system user
.I rgbeast
under systemd with a strict sandbox, publishes
.I io.github.djshiye.RGBeast1
on the system bus, checks every change with polkit, stores the last state
in
.I /var/lib/rgbeast/state.json
and re-applies it at start and after the machine wakes from sleep.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-scan
Print what would be detected and exit. Useful for support requests.
.TP
.B \-\-simulate
Serve three simulated devices instead of real hardware.
.TP
.B \-\-session
Register on the session bus instead of the system bus (development only;
polkit is skipped).
.TP
.BI \-\-state\-dir " DIR"
Keep state.json in DIR (default: $STATE_DIRECTORY, else /var/lib/rgbeast).
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-\-version
Print usage or the version and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rgbeast (1)
